  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `crates/post/tests/` had 143 flat test binaries. It now has 9 directory suites.\n- `crates/sim/tests/` had 95 flat test binaries. It now has 8 directory suites.\n- Each old file is a module of one suite (`tests/<suite>/<old name>.rs`). Its text did not change, except for these mechanical edits:\n  - `mod recorded;` and the other shared helpers (`inverted_support`, `mirror_trace`, `macro_b`, `ac_trunnion_support`) became `use crate::<helper>;`. Each suite's `main.rs` declares a helper one time, by `#[path]`.\n  - `legacy_program` (in `script_dialects`) and `coincident_arcs/reader.rs` (in `script_arcs`) are declared one time in `main.rs`. `clippy::duplicate_mod` refuses two declarations in one binary.\n  - Each relative `include_str!` / `include_bytes!` and `#[path]` path gained one `../`.\n  - A doc command `cargo test -p camcraft-post --test <old>` now reads `--test <suite> <old>::`.\n- A submodule directory with one owner moved with its owner: `agie_safe_setup`, `fanuc_post`, `heidenhain_cycles`, `sodick_ln2w`, `upright_after_tilt`, `richauto_safety` and sim `model_excess`.\n- The data directories did not move: `golden/`, `recorded/`, `klartext/`, `coincident_arcs/`. Other crates read them by path.\n- `recorded::tmp` adds a per-process counter to the temp file name. One process now runs all script modules in parallel. Two modules that post the same script and case must not write the same file.\n- `every_shipped_post_script_has_its_suite` now looks in `tests/script_goldens/`. It also checks that `main.rs` declares each script module.\n- Six `xtask` pins named old post and sim binaries. They now name the suite that holds the module (`fanuc_post` is in `script_dialects`, and so on).\n- `assets/posts/AGENTS.md` and `docs/tester-kits/fanuc-mgi-blank/README.md` name the new paths.\n\nPost suites: `script_goldens`, `script_cycles`, `script_probe`, `script_wcs`, `script_rotary`, `script_edm`, `script_dialects`, `script_arcs`, `post_engine`.\nSim suites: `stock_engines`, `stock_field`, `stock_carry`, `fixture_laws`, `reach_laws`, `gouge_laws`, `rest_credit`, `sim_timeline`.\n\nAll post suite names match `OUTPUT_SUITES` in `.github/scripts/post-merge-report.sh` (`post_engine`, `script_*`). A red post suite on main is still a wrong-output failure, and that workflow script does not change.\n\n## Cause\n\nEach flat file in `tests/` is its own binary. Each binary links the crate and its dependencies again. Issue #919 measured about 5.2 GB of disk for each worktree for these two crates.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Test list, before and after (`cargo test -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-sim --tests -- --list`): 2353 tests before and 2353 after. A script matched each old test name to exactly one new name with a module prefix: 0 missing, 0 extra.\n- `#[test]` count in the source: 1579 before (post 917, sim 662) and 1579 after.\n- Binaries: 242 test targets before, 21 after (17 suites, the 2 libs, and 2 bin targets).\n- Pin `recorded_streams::every_shipped_post_script_has_its_suite` (suite `script_goldens`):\n  - It was red after the fold and before the fix (\"has no suite .../tests/script_fanuc.rs\").\n  - Mutation: I removed `mod script_fanuc;` from `script_goldens/main.rs`. The pin was red. I restored the line. The pin was green.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on the final head: 31 steps, 0 failed (post lib, the 9 post suites, the 8 sim suites, xtask unit tests). An earlier run on the first commit also ran about 70 app suites for a `crates/post/src` comment: all green; that comment is no longer in the diff.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo test -p xtask`: 365 passed, 0 failed (with the asset and gate-map tests).\n- `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings` stops on `xtask/src/unit_sweep.rs:67` (`if` guard returns a bool literal). This PR does not touch that file. The same error is on `upstream/main`.\n- Light lane (`cargo xtask gate light --base upstream/main`): 6 steps, 0 failed.\n- Heavy lanes: `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main --dry-run` plans 0 steps. The heavy lanes cover only `HEAVY_CRATES` (kernel, motion, app). The 5 `#[ignore]`d heavy tests of sim had no heavy step before this PR, and they have none after; that is not a change. They are still in their suites (`stock_field`, `fixture_laws`, `rest_credit`) and `cargo test -- --list` lists them.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No post script, machine file or generator changed. The fold moves test sources only. The goldens and recorded streams stay at their paths, and every golden test ran green in the quick gate. I did not run the `example_catalog` suites: no post or toolpath output changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The `recorded::tmp` counter has no test of its own. A race between two modules with one tag is not deterministic, so a test cannot make it fail every time.\n- The release tier was not run. The 5 heavy-lane sim tests (`#[ignore]`d) are still in the suites. The heavy plan finds them (see above).\n- Windows and macOS were not built. The change is paths in Rust source with `/`, which all three hosts read.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nThese open PRs edit files that this PR moves. Git applies their edits to the renamed files when they merge main. A PR that adds a new flat file must move it into a suite:\n- #4395 (`script_heidenhain_klartext.rs`, `klartext/`).\n- #4387 (`script_heidenhain.rs`).\n- #4380 (`recorded/mod.rs`, different function).\n- #4371 (`setup_change.rs`, `upright_after_tilt.rs` and their directories).\n- #4298 (`tormach_lathe_post.rs`, `tormach_plasma_post.rs`).\n- #4009 (sim `undercut_laws.rs`, `verify_avoid_undercut.rs`).\n- #2646 (adds `script_hurco_winmax.rs` and other new post files). `every_shipped_post_script_has_its_suite` will ask for `script_goldens/script_hurco_winmax.rs`.\n\nWhichever merges second refreshes.\n\nFollow-up: #4420 (old test paths in code comments of `crates/post/src`, `crates/app/tests`, `crates/gcode/tests` and the GPU fixtures).\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #3188\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
